
== coffee / u_t = -k*(u - A) / random
equation: u_t = -k*(u - A)
          target u(t); fit A, k
split: random, 9 points to train, 2 held out

rank model                              held-out error    time   fitted
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
1  = PINN (neural network + equation)           0.1684    4.0s   A=1.16, k=0.02892
2  = Polynomial + equation                        0.17    3.6s   A=1.848, k=0.02921
3    Smoothing spline (data only)               0.3503    0.6s   -
4    Equation fit (classical)                   0.3649    0.7s   A=32.33, k=0.05208
5    Polynomial (data only)                     0.3704    0.0s   -
6    Neural network (data only)                 0.4849    3.1s   -

best: Polynomial + equation. Held-out error is the RMS error on data the models never saw.
=     2 models are within the noise of the lowest error on these 2 held-out points, so the data cannot tell them apart.
      The one with the fewest free numbers is returned; pick="lowest" would return PINN (neural network + equation).

